WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.619
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.919 --> 00:00:16.250
Unit six: Urban Futures. In this unit, you will discuss how cities can become sustainable and liveable.

4
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.274
megacity.

5
00:00:18.974 --> 00:00:22.588
megacity means a city with more than ten million people.

6
00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:26.037
Jakarta and Manila are megacities.

7
00:00:26.737 --> 00:00:29.877
Your turn. Say: megacity.

8
00:00:32.577 --> 00:00:33.578
megacity.

9
00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:36.107
green infrastructure.

10
00:00:36.807 --> 00:00:42.487
green infrastructure means parks, trees and wetlands used to manage water and heat in cities.

11
00:00:42.787 --> 00:00:45.750
Green infrastructure can reduce flooding.

12
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.625
Your turn. Say: green infrastructure.

13
00:00:52.325 --> 00:00:53.953
green infrastructure.

14
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.160
vertical farming.

15
00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.681
vertical farming means growing crops in stacked layers inside buildings.

16
00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:05.014
Vertical farming uses ninety percent less water.

17
00:01:05.714 --> 00:01:08.888
Your turn. Say: vertical farming.

18
00:01:11.588 --> 00:01:12.764
vertical farming.

19
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.297
mixed-use development.

20
00:01:15.997 --> 00:01:21.700
mixed-use development means a project combining homes, shops and offices in one area.

21
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.928
Mixed-use developments reduce the need to drive.

22
00:01:25.628 --> 00:01:29.105
Your turn. Say: mixed-use development.

23
00:01:31.805 --> 00:01:33.166
mixed-use development.

24
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.476
walkability.

25
00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:41.032
walkability means how easy and pleasant it is to walk in an area.

26
00:01:41.332 --> 00:01:43.819
Shaded pavements improve walkability.

27
00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:47.938
Your turn. Say: walkability.

28
00:01:50.638 --> 00:01:51.813
walkability.

29
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:54.247
urban heat island.

30
00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:59.524
urban heat island means a city area much hotter than its surroundings.

31
00:01:59.824 --> 00:02:03.078
Concrete and traffic create an urban heat island.

32
00:02:03.778 --> 00:02:07.138
Your turn. Say: urban heat island.

33
00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:11.083
urban heat island.

34
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:13.119
public realm.

35
00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:18.164
public realm means streets, squares and parks open to everyone.

36
00:02:18.464 --> 00:02:21.810
Investing in the public realm makes cities fairer.

37
00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.499
Your turn. Say: public realm.

38
00:02:28.199 --> 00:02:29.235
public realm.

39
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.286
smart grid.

40
00:02:31.986 --> 00:02:37.468
smart grid means an electricity network that uses data to manage supply efficiently.

41
00:02:37.768 --> 00:02:40.778
A smart grid can balance solar power and demand.

42
00:02:41.478 --> 00:02:44.096
Your turn. Say: smart grid.

43
00:02:46.796 --> 00:02:47.866
smart grid.

44
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.093
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:51.393 --> 00:02:53.683
Phnom Penh is getting hotter every year.

46
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:59.679
That's the urban heat island effect. Concrete has been allowed to replace trees.

47
00:03:00.983 --> 00:03:02.182
Can it be reversed?

48
00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:09.233
It's being tackled in Singapore through green infrastructure: rooftop gardens, parks and canals.

49
00:03:10.517 --> 00:03:15.187
I've read that vertical farms are expected to be built in several Asian megacities.

50
00:03:16.483 --> 00:03:20.433
Yes, and mixed-use developments are said to improve walkability.

51
00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.874
Our public realm needs to be redesigned for people, not just cars.

52
00:03:27.183 --> 00:03:30.869
Agreed. The best cities are being planned around pedestrians.

53
00:03:32.183 --> 00:03:34.659
Grammar focus: Advanced passives.

54
00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:39.373
Advanced passives include continuous and infinitive forms.

55
00:03:39.673 --> 00:03:46.032
The problem is being tackled. Farms are expected to be built. The plan is thought to have reduced traffic.

56
00:03:46.332 --> 00:03:48.482
They are typical of formal reports.

57
00:03:48.782 --> 00:03:55.054
Advanced passives are common in reports, news and academic writing about planning and policy.

58
00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:59.457
Now read and listen. Designing Cities for People.

59
00:03:59.757 --> 00:04:05.205
By 2050, nearly seven in ten people are expected to live in cities.

60
00:04:06.517 --> 00:04:10.443
Many megacities are already struggling with heat, traffic and pollution.

61
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:17.302
In some neighbourhoods, temperatures have been measured several degrees higher than in the countryside.

62
00:04:18.617 --> 00:04:25.098
Green infrastructure, such as trees and wetlands, is now being used to cool streets and absorb rainwater.

63
00:04:26.383 --> 00:04:33.259
Planners are also promoting mixed-use developments, where people can live, work and shop within walking distance.

64
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:39.324
Vertical farming is thought to have great potential for feeding dense populations.

65
00:04:40.617 --> 00:04:46.192
Meanwhile, smart grids are being installed to manage energy more efficiently.

66
00:04:47.483 --> 00:04:53.326
The cities of the future, it is argued, must be designed around people rather than cars.

67
00:04:54.617 --> 00:04:57.536
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:04:57.836 --> 00:05:00.892
A city with more than ten million people is a blank.

69
00:05:01.192 --> 00:05:05.263
A, megacity. B, smart grid. C, public realm.

70
00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.784
The answer is A: megacity.

71
00:05:13.283 --> 00:05:15.318
A new park blank at the moment.

72
00:05:15.618 --> 00:05:19.724
A, is building. B, is being built. C, has built.

73
00:05:23.717 --> 00:05:26.436
The answer is B: is being built.

74
00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.321
The bridge is expected blank next year.

75
00:05:30.621 --> 00:05:34.809
A, to complete. B, to be completed. C, completing.

76
00:05:38.817 --> 00:05:41.722
The answer is B: to be completed.

77
00:05:43.217 --> 00:05:46.052
How easy it is to walk in an area is blank.

78
00:05:46.352 --> 00:05:52.026
A, walkability. B, vertical farming. C, green infrastructure.

79
00:05:56.017 --> 00:05:58.782
The answer is A: walkability.

80
00:06:00.283 --> 00:06:04.152
According to the text, what is being used to cool streets?

81
00:06:04.452 --> 00:06:10.996
A, air conditioning. B, green infrastructure. C, smart grids.

82
00:06:14.983 --> 00:06:17.819
The answer is B: green infrastructure.

83
00:06:19.317 --> 00:06:24.349
Now it's your turn. Part one: How could Phnom Penh become a more liveable city?

84
00:06:29.649 --> 00:06:34.598
Part two: Propose two changes and explain how each would help residents.

85
00:06:40.898 --> 00:06:53.465
First, more shade trees should be planted along major roads to reduce heat; second, mixed-use neighbourhoods should be encouraged so that people can walk to work. Together, these would cut traffic and improve health.

86
00:06:53.765 --> 00:06:55.927
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:06:56.917 --> 00:07:01.798
Great work today! You learned eight new words and advanced passives.

88
00:07:02.098 --> 00:07:05.853
Today's value is community. Help the people in your town.

89
00:07:06.153 --> 00:07:08.759
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

90
00:07:09.059 --> 00:07:12.141
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

